   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The `ASLS` is a robust baseline correction method that finds the smooth lower envelope of a spectrum by penalizing <br>\n",
    "positive peaks less than negative ones. It is one of the best choices when dealing with RFI in radio astronomy, <br>\n",
    " since it suppresses the bandpass trend while preserving the spikes you want to detect.\n",
    "\n",
    " What is ASLS?\n",
    "\n",
    "ASLS = Asymmetric Least Squares smoothing\n",
    "\n",
    "* It is a baseline correction algorithm that models the spectrum as a smooth baseline + peaks and tries to fit only the smooth part.\n",
    "\n",
    "* It works by penalizing deviations asymmetrically:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Negative deviations (data below the baseline) are penalized strongly.\n",
    "\n",
    "* Positive deviations (peaks above the baseline, e.g. RFI spikes or spectral lines) are penalized weakly.\n",
    "\n",
    "This ensures that the fitted curve follows the lower envelope of the spectrum, ignoring sharp upward peaks."
   ]
  },
